ADR-038: Dashboard Scoped to orgId + applicationId

STATUS: Accepted

CONTEXT:
Dashboard model stored userId + organizationId (string) + applicationId (optional).
This caused a fetch mismatch: saved with userId 'admin' but request context returned
different string → list returned 0 dashboards.
Platform hierarchy is Org → Application → Device/Workflow → Dashboard.
Dashboards display derived device state — no natural per-user ownership exists.

DECISION:
Remove userId entirely. Replace organizationId (string) with orgId (ObjectId).
Make applicationId required. Dashboards are application-level shared resources,
consistent with Device and Workflow models.
Remove isShared / sharedWith fields (no user ownership = no per-user sharing).
Add requireAuth preHandler to all dashboard routes.
orgId always comes from JWT via getRequestContext — never from request body.

SCHEMA CHANGE:
  Before: userId (string, required), organizationId (string), applicationId (optional)
  After:  orgId (ObjectId, required), applicationId (string, required)
  Index:  { orgId, dashboardId } unique  (was { userId, dashboardId })
          { orgId, applicationId }       (was { organizationId, dashboardId })

CONSEQUENCES:
+ Consistent with Device/Workflow multi-tenancy model
+ Fixes dashboard fetch bug permanently
+ Application delete guard now orgId-safe
- Existing dashboard documents in MongoDB need migration (drop userId/organizationId,
  set orgId ObjectId, mark applicationId) — one-time operation for POC
